  notes: "WINDOWS touch / Microsoft Surface defaults (unit: effective pixel, 1/96
    inch at 100% display scaling).\n\nMicrosoft publishes no touch thresholds in ms
    or distances (only target sizes: 40x40 epx minimum). ALMOST EVERYTHING HERE IS
    A GUESS - check on a Surface (plan.md Q2, Q9).\n\nREPLACED AT RUNTIME when policy.useOsValues
    is on: doubleTapTimeoutMs (GetDoubleClickTime; this is the mouse setting, the
    separate touch double-tap speed is not read yet). Density comes from GetDpiForWindow
    (display scaling x 96).\n\nNOT READ YET (Q9): the touch accessibility settings
    under HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Wisp\\Touch (press-and-hold time, touch double-tap
    speed, spatial tolerance) - value names and units need checking.\n\nGUESSES:\n-
    fallbackDpi 192: 200% scaling, typical for a Surface.\n- doubleTapTimeoutMs 500:
    Windows' default double-click time.\n- touchSlopDp 8, longPressTimeoutMs 500.\n-
    doubleTapMinTimeMs 40, doubleTapSlopDp 100, multiFingerTapWindowMs 150.\n- minFlingVelocityDps
    50, maxFlingVelocityDps 8000, velocityWindowMs 100.\n- swipeAngleToleranceDeg 30,
    minRotationDeg 5, minScalingSpanDp 170, edgeSlopDp 12.\n\nQ11 (whether Windows
    recognises a double tap on the 2nd finger down or up) belongs to the WindowsDoubleTap
    gesture asset (phase 5); assumed: up."
